        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "8787b2f4-c27a-3e63-bdb4-c5902056ffad",
                "word": "lymphome",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ea667d68-026a-44c6-8ff5-7f4872b913a3",
                        "entry_id": "8787b2f4-c27a-3e63-bdb4-c5902056ffad",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "lymphomes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8099d7ad-c7ae-3867-a85e-c86492741198",
                        "entry_id": "8787b2f4-c27a-3e63-bdb4-c5902056ffad",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tumeur composée de tissu adénoïde typique, c'est-à-dire tumeur d’un tissu ou d’un organe lymphoïde."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca00bc45-ba8d-491b-8b47-a041bf92ed1b",
                                "sense_id": "8099d7ad-c7ae-3867-a85e-c86492741198",
                                "text": "D’autres types de tumeurs oculaires (mélanome, carcinome ou lymphome) peuvent se développer dans la conjonctive, les paupières ou l’orbite."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5ae828a-3618-4614-8ee2-72b1202564e2",
                                "sense_id": "8099d7ad-c7ae-3867-a85e-c86492741198",
                                "text": "Les perforations sont rares, de 0,1 à 0,3 % des procédures, avec un risque majoré en cas d’entéroscopie par voie basse, de sténose liée à une maladie de Crohn, d’anastomose intestinale récente ou de lymphome traité par radiothérapie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "093371e1-fb22-43e2-84b3-d0c7c0172f24",
                                "sense_id": "8099d7ad-c7ae-3867-a85e-c86492741198",
                                "text": "Le don de sang permet de soigner de nombreuses maladies et de nombreux cancers tels que leucémies, lymphomes, myélomes…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f7074977-03d8-4219-b122-6429926f6c11",
                        "source_entry_id": "8787b2f4-c27a-3e63-bdb4-c5902056ffad",
                        "source_sense_id": "8099d7ad-c7ae-3867-a85e-c86492741198",
                        "target_lang_word": "lymphoma",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lymphoma",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e6b0be5-548c-3eeb-b2a3-36315b1db832",
                                        "entry_id": "9fcd28ff-24fc-37d0-8523-3a9812ee11bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A malignant tumor that arises in the lymph nodes or in other lymphoid tissue."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6e888a6-f3e8-4872-a1ca-23d4a06079a0",
                                                "sense_id": "6e6b0be5-548c-3eeb-b2a3-36315b1db832",
                                                "text": "In the one sub-class, we have the Leukaemic Lymphoma, the Typhous Lymphoma, the Hyperplastic Lymphoma (ex. the simple hypertrophied tonsil), Lympho-sarcoma, Scrofulous Glands; and in the other sub-class, Tubercle of man, and Perlsucht or Parresyge, or Morbus Gallicus, the pearl distemper of ruminating animals."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a348cc6-4a7d-4155-bcbe-aa6aef1cb2ad",
                                                "sense_id": "6e6b0be5-548c-3eeb-b2a3-36315b1db832",
                                                "text": "Common immunohistochemical markers of this lymphoma include CD2, CD56, CD3, and T-cell receptors. 7 Typically, the histology of these lymphomas are characterized by monomorphic inflammatory cellular infiltrates, which may be diffuse or show angiocentricity and angiodestruction as well as tissue destruction. 7 Lymphoid markers from the nasal mucosal biopsy from this patient were negative for CD56 and EBER."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
